{"name":"Tatarian Aster","hex":"#976e9a","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aster","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several plants of the genus Aster; one of its flowers.","A star-shaped structure formed during the mitosis of a cell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aster"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aster tataricus","blocks":[{"text":"Aster tataricus, also called Tatarian aster and Tatarinow's aster, is a member of the Aster genus of flowering plants native to East Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Aster_Tataricus.JPG/330px-Aster_Tataricus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aster_tataricus","wikidata":"Q189368"},{"title":"Aster (genus)","blocks":[{"text":"Aster is a genus of perennial flowering plants in the family Asteraceae. Its circumscription has been narrowed, and it now encompasses around 170 species, all but one of which are restricted to Eurasia; many species formerly in Aster are now in other genera of the tribe Astereae. Aster amellus is the type species of the genus and the family Asteraceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Asteraceae_-_Aster_amellus.JPG/330px-Asteraceae_-_Aster_amellus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aster_(genus)","wikidata":"Q517130"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Aster_Tataricus.JPG/500px-Aster_Tataricus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Aster_Tataricus.JPG/1280px-Aster_Tataricus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Aster_Tataricus.JPG/500px-Aster_Tataricus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=p